Q*) .What is upcasting/downcasting? output ke sath


Upcasting
Upcasting = Child object ko Parent class ke reference se refer karna.

***************

class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Animal a = new Dog();   // Upcasting                //Animal → reference type (Parent)
                                                          //Dog → actual object (Child)
        a.sound();                     //Child object is stored/referenced by Parent reference.
    }                                     //Upcasting is generally automatic.
}

*****************Output
Animal makes sound



*********************************2. Downcasting
Downcasting = Parent reference ko Child class ke reference mein convert karna.


class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Animal a = new Dog();       // Upcasting

        Dog d = (Dog) a;            // Downcasting

        d.sound();
        d.bark();
    }
}

***************Output
Animal makes sound
Dog barks




**************************************Interview answer

Upcasting is converting a child-class reference into a parent-class reference. It is implicit and provides access to the parent-class members. 

Downcasting is converting a parent-class reference back into a child-class reference. It requires explicit casting and should be done carefully because an invalid downcast causes ClassCastException.



