Q11) What is method overriding ?

Method overriding occurs when a child class provides its own implementation of a method that is already defined in the parent class.

overriding called runtime polymorphism

*******************"Why is overriding called runtime polymorphism?"

Because when an overridden method is called through a parent reference, the implementation that executes is determined at runtime based on the actual object.

*************************Simple trick:

Same method + parent-child + child gives new implementation = Overriding


************************Basic example :
    
class Animal {

    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal makes sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {

    @Override
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}

******************************* Main :

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Dog d = new Dog();

        d.sound();
    }
}

*******************************Output:
Dog barks


